  "cover_text": "The court system in Sheridan, Arkansas is a government entity that governs the intersections of those government-enacted laws put within its jurisdiction. No other agency within the government can monitor those areas the way the Sheridan court does. The Sheridan legal system incorporates not only the state, but every county in the state as it applies different branches of government to make decisions in areas of criminal, juvenile and civil law. At the same time, it handles infractions to roads and law enforcement laws. The court portion affects decisions in various cases that are governed by the Sheridan criminal justice system, and the court with other courts in Arkansas that are governed by the same laws.\nThe Sheridan legal record is maintained in a fully bilingual daily newspaper issued in two versions, each providing subscriber with a reader-friendly version in their native language and a more comprehensive version in English. These",
